    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What is the most famous dish at Wimbledon*? "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Strawberries",
            "ref": "v-strawberry"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and cream!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Wimbledon is the oldest of the four Grand Slams*. It was first played in London in 1877. Strawberries were in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "season",
            "zh": "当季"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tournament",
            "zh": "锦标赛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was being played. And in Victorian* England, they had become a fashionable thing to eat. So, the red soft fruit "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "took root",
            "ref": "v-take-root"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at Wimbledon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "How did strawberries and cream "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "come about",
            "zh": "产生"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? They were first served together in 1509 in a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "banquet",
            "ref": "v-banquet"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". At that time, rich people ate strawberries as part of their afternoon tea. Cream was part of a poor man’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "diet",
            "ref": "v-diet"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". So, strawberries and cream brought together the rich and the poor. The dish was served at the first Wimbledon and became a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "hit",
            "zh": "热门"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, people can buy many dishes when they watch a tennis match at Wimbledon. But a bowl of strawberries and cream is the best!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*温布尔登网球锦标赛（The Championships, Wimbledon），简称“温网”。它是一项历史悠久、极具声望的世界性网球赛事，也是四大满贯中唯一的草地比赛，举办时间通常为每年6月或7月，举办地在英国伦敦郊区的温布尔登。"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*大满贯（Grand Slam），即大赛、大奖赛。网球四大满贯包括澳大利亚网球公开赛（Australian Open）、法国网球公开赛（French Open）、温布尔登网球锦标赛（Wimbledon）和美国网球公开赛（US Open）。"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*维多利亚时代（the Victorian era），指1837年至1901年英国维多利亚女王统治时期，常被视为大英帝国的黄金时代。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
